    "sha": "177c2ba39689b0450bf5de89d23ed5894cf8bd5f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDE3N2MyYmEzOTY4OWIwNDUwYmY1ZGU4OWQyM2VkNTg5NGNmOGJkNWY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-21T01:04:18Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-21T01:04:18Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim): read the first traverse through every pose of the work-turning rotaries\n\nThe post sends Z, then X/Y, then the move with the rotary words, so the\nX/Y traverse runs with each work-turning rotary where the previous\nprogram left it. A new law, verify::first_traverse_low_posed, reads the\nstart stock, the part and the tagged steel through every such pose: on\nthe sphere about the WCS origin when two or more rotaries turn the\nwork, a full turn about the one line otherwise (the lines pass through\nthe WCS origin, the index-swing setup law). It reads a rotary kind on a\nmachine where two rotaries turn the work, and a multi-axis kind on a\nmachine whose table tilts. A lone work-turning rotary with no usable\nline refuses generation by name. The op stamp of a newly judged\noperation takes the word first-traverse-posed-3084.\n\nStacked on #3099. Decision: docs/decisions/3084-posed-first-traverse.md.\n\nFixes #3084\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "bd4dfc2eba505c84246cd0e1658260954e0f0fa7",
